{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1471625-exigent-exalted-and-gods-of-nothing","id":1471625,"title":"Exigent Exalted and Gods of Nothing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-01T16:03:02-08:00","id":1471625,"title":"Exigent Exalted and Gods of Nothing","content":"Suppose, hypothetically, a god whose portfolio was erased (by the Wyld, the Three Spheres Cataclysm, etc.) manages to obtain an Exigent. Would the Exigent's powers be reflective of the god's portfolio as it was, or on whatever scraps of power the god currently maintains?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T17:32:55-08:00","id":1471635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1471625-exigent-exalted-and-gods-of-nothing#post1471625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose, hypothetically, a god whose portfolio was erased (by the Wyld, the Three Spheres Cataclysm, etc.) manages to obtain an Exigent. Would the Exigent's powers be reflective of the god's portfolio as it was, or on whatever scraps of power the god currently maintains?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess it depends on the kind of deity it was. If he was a terrestrial one, its portfolio would be a place or landmark, something with material heft and whose <b><i>concept of</i></b> would sort of exist even if the specific example a deity was steward of is gone. So even though, let's say, Omlaut of Diorite Spires, is gone from Creation along with the Mount Murang it was carved upon, cities, carved from the body of mountains or not, are still a known quantity in Creation and consequently the deity's charms would still have meaning and identity to draw on, though much diminished by its divine steward's loss.<br /> <br /> Now, if we are speaking of a fallen celestial deity, one that was connected to an abstract concept, well, <b><i>there</i></b> you might have a problem indeed, because the deity losing its portfolio implies <b><i>that concept is no more</i></b> and if such is the case how does one personify/represent <i><b>something that does not exist</b></i>? That is a sure road for incomprehensible things and madness indeed, depending on how close or distant was the lost purview to still existing concepts.<br /> <br /> Now, about if an Exigent's powers would be reflective of the god's portfolio as it was, or on whatever scraps of power the god currently maintains - i would say, based on the fluff of the sample exigent we get in the corebook (that of Wu Jian's city-god), a bit of column A, a bit of column B. An Exigence can be considered as magnifying lens of sorts, in that it not only makes an image clearer, but makes minute details more visible and amplify's one scope.<br /> <br /> An Exigent would <i><b>start </b></i>reflecting the god as is, but with luck to survive and grow might mature into its power and, through the sun-borne potential hidden within, start to see nuances of concept, essence and scale that expand from its patron surface to its past depths and from there to even broader vistas of connected concepts and so on perhaps. Much like the Exigent of Wu Jian when she exalts has glimpses of the whole of the city's history, then of the Goddess of the Shining Metropolis, the ultimate city-deity above all and from there of Yu-shan, the primordial conception of a center of civilization before there was even a world, itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-31-2026, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T00:38:00-07:00","id":1508715,"title":"","content":"If the deity in question was associated with a non-material concept that no longer exists, then we have a serious dilemma on our hands; after all, it is impossible to give a human face to an idea that doesn't exist.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><a href=\"https://trapthemouse.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">trap the mouse</span></a></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27673-manisla","name":"Manisla","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T21:22:48-07:00","id":1535095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1471625-exigent-exalted-and-gods-of-nothing?p=1508715#post1508715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the deity in question was associated with a non-material concept that no longer exists, then we have a serious dilemma on our hands; after all, it is impossible to give a human face to an idea that doesn't exist.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><a href=\"https://trapthemouse.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#ffffff\">trap the mouse</span></a></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Except the concept <b>once </b>existed and so <i>already </i>has a face, though its role is little more than a memory. That an idea or concept disappears from human society and imagination does <b>NOT </b>have to mean it's gone forever (unless some high-level weirdness or sorcerous workings are at play).Texts, poems or songs kept only by memory can exist and they may rise curiosity or inspire those who hear them - lost writings or objects buried by the sands of time can be unhearthed and spur rediscovery. Dead people who knew epochs of different standards may teach of things long lost to the living. Close or related concepts may provide perspective &amp; points of reference.<br /> <br /> Also gods can change purviews as shown quite clearly by Ahlat's backstory in Houses of the Bull God, so as big or small a deal to one's confidence, self and identity as losing a job, i guess.<br /> <br /> A god diminished can still find ways fair &amp; foul to climb its path back into glories past if one has the will, confidence, contacts and luck to attempt to leave a mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-05-2024, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}